    "status": "present",
    "value": "Words are at most 7 letters, so each word has at most 7 prefixes and 7 suffixes, i.e. at most 49 prefix/suffix pairs. During construction, insert the key prefix + '#' + suffix for every pair into a hash map, overwriting the stored index as words are processed in order, so the map keeps the largest index. A query then builds the same key and does one lookup. The separator '#' cannot occur in a word, so different (prefix, suffix) pairs never collide."
  },
